  "review": false,
  "text": "**English**\n\n- **Date:** Sangam texts are generally dated between the 3rd century BCE and the 3rd century CE. Greco-Roman references, Tamil-Brahmi inscriptions and Ashoka's mention of the Cheras, Cholas and Pandyas support this (p. 38). The poems were composed early and compiled into anthologies later.\n- **Four kinds of source** (p. 33):\n  1. Classical Tamil literature\n  2. Epigraphy\n  3. Archaeological excavations and material culture\n  4. Non-Tamil and foreign texts\n- **Thinai:** a concept from the *Tholkappiyam*. The five landscapes are:\n  - **Kurinji** – hills\n  - **Mullai** – forest and pasture\n  - **Marutham** – fertile river valley\n  - **Neythal** – coast\n  - **Paalai** – arid land"
